-- title:
--   The space $\mathcal V$, $\mathcal P(\mathcal C^d\times\mathcal V)$ and its marginal flows, the limit realizations (i)–(v), the context of §5.5, $\mathcal A^c_{\rm semi}$ and the controls (5.13)
-- statement:
--   This file collects the objects of Section 5 of the paper.
--
--   1. **The space $\mathcal V$** (§5.2): the measures $q$ on $[0,T]\times A$ whose first marginal is Lebesgue measure, with the topology of weak convergence. For $q\in\mathcal V$ we write $\int_0^t\int_A F(s,a)\,q_s(da)\,ds$ for the integral of $F$ against $q$ restricted to $\{(s,a):s\le t\}$.
--   2. **$\mathcal P(\mathcal C^d\times\mathcal V)$** with its weak topology and Borel $\sigma$-field, and the **marginal flow** of $\bar{\boldsymbol\mu}\in\mathcal P(\mathcal C^d\times\mathcal V)$: $\mu_t=\bar{\boldsymbol\mu}\circ[(x,q)\mapsto x_t]^{-1}$ (footnote 7).
--   3. **Limit realizations.** For a $\mathcal P(A)$-valued semi-Markov $\Lambda^*$, processes $X$, $W$ and a flow $\mu$ on a probability space satisfy (i)–(v) of Theorem 5.4 if: (i) $X_0$, $W$, $\mu$ are independent; (ii) $W$ is a Brownian motion with respect to the completed filtration generated by $(X_0,\mu_t,W_t)$; (iii) $X$ is continuous, adapted to that filtration, and $X_0\sim\lambda$; (iv) $dX_t=\int_A b(t,X_t,\mu_t,a)\Lambda^*(t,X_t,\mu)(da)dt+dW_t$; (v) for each $t$, $\mu_t=\mathcal L(X_t\mid\mathcal F^\mu_t)$ a.s.
--   4. **The average payoff** $\frac1n\sum_{i=1}^nJ^n_i(\alpha)$.
--   5. **The context of §5.5** (p. 30): a sequence of $n$-player profiles with solutions, a subsequence $n_k$ along which the laws of $\mu^{n_k}$ converge to the law of a flow $\mu$, and a probability space carrying $\mu$, $X$, $W$ satisfying (i)–(v) for a semi-Markov $\Lambda^*$, together with the value identity (5.8)
--   $$\lim_{k\to\infty}\frac1{n_k}\sum_{i=1}^{n_k}J^{n_k}_i(\alpha^{n_k})=\mathbb E\Big[\int_0^T\int_A f(t,X_t,\mu_t,a)\Lambda^*(t,X_t,\mu)(da)\,dt+g(X_T,\mu_T)\Big].$$
--   6. **$\mathcal A^c_{\rm semi}$**: the continuous $A$-valued semi-Markov functions $\beta:[0,T]\times\mathbb R^d\times C([0,T];\mathcal P(\mathbb R^d))\to A$.
--   7. **The controls (5.13)**: for $\beta\in\mathcal A^c_{\rm semi}$ and a player $k$, $\beta^{n,k}(t,x)=\beta\big(t,x^k_t,\frac1n\sum_{j=1}^n\delta_{x^j}\big)$, where the empirical measure of the paths acts through its flow $t\mapsto\frac1n\sum_j\delta_{x^j_t}$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** In $\mathcal V$ the first-marginal condition is that the push-forward of $q$ to $\mathbb R$ by $(s,a)\mapsto s$ is Lebesgue measure restricted to $[0,T]$; $q$ ranges over finite measures with the weak topology of `FiniteMeasure`, and no disintegration $q_t(da)$ is used anywhere. The marginal at time $t$ is the push-forward by the (continuous, hence measurable) evaluation. Sequences of $n$-player games are indexed so that term $n$ is the game with $n+1$ players; an index shift changes no limit. The completed filtration in (ii)–(iii) is the one of the `Model` file. In the §5.5 context, "the subsequence converges in law to $\mu$" is stated as convergence of the laws to a probability measure equal to the law of $\mu$.
-- source:
--   Lacker, On the convergence of closed-loop Nash equilibria to the mean field game limit, arXiv:1808.02745v1, p. 25, §5.2; p. 26, footnote 7; p. 28, Theorem 5.4 (i)–(v), (5.8); pp. 30–31, §5.5, (5.13)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ClosedLoopMFG_Limit_Model
import Definitions.Def_ClosedLoopMFG_Limit_Game
import Definitions.Def_ClosedLoopMFG_Limit_Equilibrium

namespace ClosedLoopMFG.Limit

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Topology
open scoped ENNReal NNReal

/-- The space `V` (§5.2, p. 25): measures `q` on `[0, T] × A` whose first marginal is Lebesgue
measure on `[0, T]`, with the topology of weak convergence (the subspace topology of
`FiniteMeasure`) and its Borel σ-field. -/
def V (T : ℝ≥0) {EA : Type} [TopologicalSpace EA] [MeasurableSpace EA] [OpensMeasurableSpace EA]
    (A : Set EA) : Type :=
  {q : FiniteMeasure (Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) T × A) //
    (q : Measure (Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) T × A)).map (fun p => (p.1 : ℝ)) =
      volume.restrict (Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) T)}

instance instTopologicalSpaceV (T : ℝ≥0) {EA : Type} [TopologicalSpace EA] [MeasurableSpace EA]
    [OpensMeasurableSpace EA] (A : Set EA) : TopologicalSpace (V T A) :=
  inferInstanceAs (TopologicalSpace {q : FiniteMeasure (Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) T × A) //
    (q : Measure (Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) T × A)).map (fun p => (p.1 : ℝ)) =
      volume.restrict (Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) T)})

instance instMeasurableSpaceV (T : ℝ≥0) {EA : Type} [TopologicalSpace EA] [MeasurableSpace EA]
    [OpensMeasurableSpace EA] (A : Set EA) : MeasurableSpace (V T A) :=
  borel _

instance instBorelSpaceV (T : ℝ≥0) {EA : Type} [TopologicalSpace EA] [MeasurableSpace EA]
    [OpensMeasurableSpace EA] (A : Set EA) : BorelSpace (V T A) :=
  ⟨rfl⟩

/-- A point of `V` as a measure on `[0, T] × A`. -/
noncomputable def V.meas {T : ℝ≥0} {EA : Type} [TopologicalSpace EA] [MeasurableSpace EA]
    [OpensMeasurableSpace EA] {A : Set EA} (q : V T A) : Measure (Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) T × A) :=
  (q.1 : Measure (Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) T × A))

/-- `∫_0^t ∫_A F(s, a) q_s(da) ds`, written as the integral of `F` against `q` restricted to
`{(s, a) : s ≤ t}` (no disintegration of `q` is needed). -/
noncomputable def qInt {T : ℝ≥0} {EA : Type} [TopologicalSpace EA] [MeasurableSpace EA]
    [OpensMeasurableSpace EA] {A : Set EA} (q : V T A) (t : ℝ) (F : ℝ → EA → ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ∫ p in {p : Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) T × A | (p.1 : ℝ) ≤ t}, F (p.1 : ℝ) (p.2 : EA) ∂q.meas

/-- `P(𝒞^d × V)` (§5.4, p. 24), with the weak topology and its Borel σ-field. -/
abbrev PCV (d : ℕ) (T : ℝ≥0) {EA : Type} [TopologicalSpace EA] [MeasurableSpace EA]
    [OpensMeasurableSpace EA] (A : Set EA) : Type :=
  Prob (Path d T × V T A)

/-- The time-`t` marginal `m̄ ∘ [(x, q) ↦ x_t]^{-1} ∈ P(ℝ^d)` of `m̄ ∈ P(𝒞^d × V)`
(footnote 7, p. 26). -/
noncomputable def margAt {d : ℕ} {T : ℝ≥0} {EA : Type} [TopologicalSpace EA]
    [MeasurableSpace EA] [OpensMeasurableSpace EA] {A : Set EA} (m : PCV d T A)
    (t : Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) T) : PR d :=
  (⟨m.meas.map (fun p : Path d T × V T A => p.1 t),
    Measure.isProbabilityMeasure_map
      ((continuous_eval_const t).measurable.comp measurable_fst).aemeasurable⟩ :
    ProbabilityMeasure (E d))

/-- The common conclusions (i)–(v) of Lemma 5.3(c) and Theorem 5.4 (pp. 26, 28), for processes
`X`, `W` and a flow `μ` on a probability space and a `P(A)`-valued semi-Markov `Λ*`:
(i) `X_0`, `W`, `μ` are independent; (ii) `W` is a Brownian motion with respect to the completed
filtration generated by `(X_0, μ_t, W_t)`; (iii) `X` is continuous, adapted to that completed
filtration, with `X_0 ∼ λ`; (iv) `dX_t = ∫_A b(t, X_t, μ_t, a) Λ*(t, X_t, μ)(da) dt + dW_t`;
(v) for each `t`, `μ_t = L(X_t | 𝓕^μ_t)` a.s. -/
def IsRelaxedRealization {Ω : Type} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {d : ℕ} {T : ℝ≥0} {EA : Type}
    [MeasurableSpace EA] {A : Set EA} (lam : PR d) (b : ℝ → E d → PR d → EA → E d)
    (Λ : ℝ → E d → Flow d T → PA A) (P : Measure Ω) (W : ℝ≥0 → Ω → E d) (X : Ω → Path d T)
    (μ : Ω → Flow d T) : Prop :=
  IsProbabilityMeasure P ∧ Measurable μ ∧ Measurable X ∧
  iIndep ![MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => ev (X ω) 0) inferInstance,
    MeasurableSpace.comap μ inferInstance, MeasurableSpace.comap (bmPath W) inferInstance] P ∧
  IsBMWrt (genFilt P (fun ω => ev (X ω) 0) W μ) P W ∧
  (∀ s : Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) T,
    Measurable[genFilt P (fun ω => ev (X ω) 0) W μ (s : ℝ).toNNReal] (fun ω => X ω s)) ∧
  P.map (fun ω => ev (X ω) 0) = lam.meas ∧
  SolvesState P W X μ (relaxDrift b Λ) ∧
  IsConsistent P X μ

/-- The average payoff `(1/n) ∑_{i=1}^n J^n_i(α)` of the `n`-player game, computed on a solution
(players indexed by `Fin (n + 1)`, i.e. `n + 1` players). -/
noncomputable def avgPayoff {n d : ℕ} {T : ℝ≥0} {lam : PR d} {EA : Type}
    {B : Fin (n + 1) → ℝ → (Fin (n + 1) → Path d T) → E d} (S : NSol (n + 1) d T lam B)
    (f : ℝ → E d → PR d → EA → ℝ) (g : E d → PR d → ℝ)
    (α : Fin (n + 1) → ℝ → (Fin (n + 1) → Path d T) → EA) : ℝ :=
  (1 / ((n : ℝ) + 1)) * ∑ i, S.J f g α i

/-- The **standing context of §5.5** (p. 30): `μ^{n_k} = μ^{n_k}[α^{n_k}]` (term `n` of the
sequence is the `(n+1)`-player game) converges in law along the subsequence `n_k = φ k` to the law
of the flow `μ`, which lives on a probability space carrying `X` and `W` that satisfy (i)–(v) of
Theorem 5.4 for the semi-Markov `Λ*`, together with the value identity (5.8). -/
def IsSec55Context {d : ℕ} {T : ℝ≥0} {EA : Type} [TopologicalSpace EA] [MeasurableSpace EA]
    [OpensMeasurableSpace EA] {A : Set EA}
    (lam : PR d) (b : ℝ → E d → PR d → EA → E d) (f : ℝ → E d → PR d → EA → ℝ)
    (g : E d → PR d → ℝ) (α : (n : ℕ) → Fin (n + 1) → ℝ → (Fin (n + 1) → Path d T) → EA)
    (S : (n : ℕ) → NSol (n + 1) d T lam (drift b (α n))) (φ : ℕ → ℕ)
    {Ω : Type} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω) (W : ℝ≥0 → Ω → E d) (X : Ω → Path d T)
    (μ : Ω → Flow d T) (Λstar : ℝ → E d → Flow d T → PA A) : Prop :=
  StrictMono φ ∧
  (∃ ν : ProbabilityMeasure (Flow d T), (ν : Measure (Flow d T)) = P.map μ ∧
    Tendsto (fun k => (S (φ k)).law) atTop (𝓝 ν)) ∧
  IsSemiMarkov Λstar ∧
  IsRelaxedRealization lam b Λstar P W X μ ∧
  Tendsto (fun k => avgPayoff (S (φ k)) f g (α (φ k))) atTop
    (𝓝 (reward P X μ (relaxRun f Λstar) g))

/-- `𝒜^c_semi` (§5.5, p. 31): continuous `A`-valued semi-Markov functions
`β : [0, T] × ℝ^d × C([0, T]; P(ℝ^d)) → A`. -/
def IsContSemiMarkovCtrl {d : ℕ} {T : ℝ≥0} {EA : Type} [TopologicalSpace EA]
    [MeasurableSpace EA] (A : Set EA) (β : ℝ → E d → Flow d T → EA) : Prop :=
  IsSemiMarkovCtrl A β ∧
  ContinuousOn (fun p : ℝ × E d × Flow d T => β p.1 p.2.1 p.2.2)
    (Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) T ×ˢ Set.univ ×ˢ Set.univ)

/-- The `n`-player control (5.13), p. 31: `β^{n,k}(t, x) = β(t, x^k_t, (1/n) ∑_j δ_{x^j})`,
where `(1/n) ∑_j δ_{x^j}` acts through its measure flow `t ↦ (1/n) ∑_j δ_{x^j_t}`. -/
noncomputable def betaNK {d n : ℕ} [NeZero n] {T : ℝ≥0} {EA : Type}
    (β : ℝ → E d → Flow d T → EA) (k : Fin n) : ℝ → (Fin n → Path d T) → EA :=
  fun t x => β t (ev (x k) t) (empFlow x)

end ClosedLoopMFG.Limit


